WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.028 --> 00:00:05.030
"Wow, there are a lot of people here," Cole said.

2
00:00:05.050 --> 00:00:06.170
"I know."

3
00:00:06.230 --> 00:00:07.791
Maggie sounded happy.

4
00:00:07.831 --> 00:00:15.496
"We might need to make more lemonade."

5
00:00:15.596 --> 00:00:35.362
Henry It had been Maggie's idea to set up their lemonade stand at the park for Belltown Arts

6
00:00:35.402 --> 00:00:38.763
Day. She'd thought they would make lots of money.

7
00:00:39.723 --> 00:00:40.923
And it looked like she was right.

8
00:00:41.604 --> 00:00:43.784
The stand had been busy all morning long.

9
00:00:44.765 --> 00:00:47.585
Belltown Arts Day was a popular tradition in Belltown.

10
00:00:48.566 --> 00:00:52.167
It was a whole day of art, music, and crafts for all ages.

11
00:00:53.247 --> 00:00:55.328
There was a crafts fair at one end of the park.

12
00:00:56.364 --> 00:01:00.866
People had set up booths there to display crafts like glassblowing and basket weaving.

13
00:01:03.047 --> 00:01:07.029
At the other end of the park, right in front of the Belltown Museum of Art, was an

14
00:01:07.109 --> 00:01:07.589
art show.

15
00:01:08.690 --> 00:01:12.551
Anyone could enter a painting, sculpture, or other piece of art in the show.

16
00:01:13.532 --> 00:01:17.273
That afternoon a committee of experts was going to judge all the pieces.

17
00:01:18.374 --> 00:01:22.616
The pieces that won first place would be displayed in the museum for the rest of the year.

18
00:01:23.808 --> 00:01:28.629
The bandstand in the middle of the park featured a full schedule of musical acts and dance groups.

19
00:01:29.690 --> 00:01:32.230
Right now a fiddler was playing a lively tune.

20
00:01:33.191 --> 00:01:37.012
Henry, Maggie, and Cole had set up the lemonade stand near the bandstand.

21
00:01:38.012 --> 00:01:39.872
Cole tapped his foot along with the music.

22
00:01:40.553 --> 00:01:42.633
"Here come some more customers," he said.

23
00:01:43.613 --> 00:01:48.635
For the next few minutes, The Lemonade Detectives stayed busy pouring lemonade and collecting money.

24
00:01:49.595 --> 00:01:52.876
When the last customer wandered off, Henry turned to his friends.

25
00:01:54.000 --> 00:01:56.022
"We should look for Nathan," he said.

26
00:01:56.042 --> 00:01:59.285
"I want to see his painting before the judging starts."

27
00:02:00.325 --> 00:02:01.747
"Me too," Cole agreed.

28
00:02:01.767 --> 00:02:03.748
"I heard it's really good."

29
00:02:04.869 --> 00:02:06.971
Their friend Nathan was a talented artist.

30
00:02:07.612 --> 00:02:09.853
This was his first year entering the art show.

31
00:02:10.774 --> 00:02:13.576
He was competing in the Age 12 and Under category.

32
00:02:14.437 --> 00:02:17.139
The other two categories were for teenagers and adults.

33
00:02:18.240 --> 00:02:19.241
Maggie looked around.

34
00:02:19.261 --> 00:02:22.344
"I guess we can take a short break," she said.

35
00:02:23.292 --> 00:02:24.953
"I want to see Nathan's painting too.

36
00:02:25.533 --> 00:02:28.374
His little sister, Nora, can't stop talking about it."

37
00:02:29.494 --> 00:02:30.234
Cole laughed.

38
00:02:30.934 --> 00:02:32.795
"Nora can never stop talking!"

39
00:02:33.055 --> 00:02:33.555
he joked.

40
00:02:33.575 --> 00:02:37.056
"She talks more than any other little kid I know."

41
00:02:38.016 --> 00:02:40.417
The Lemonade Detectives set out a Closed sign.

42
00:02:41.397 --> 00:02:43.938
Then they headed across the crowded park to the art show.

43
00:02:44.918 --> 00:02:47.279
They found Nathan standing in front of his painting.

44
00:02:48.439 --> 00:02:50.760
Nora was sitting on the ground, playing with a doll.

45
00:02:51.688 --> 00:02:53.970
Nathan's mom was chatting with a friend nearby.

46
00:02:54.950 --> 00:02:58.433
Nathan was talking to a red-haired boy named Patrick and his parents.

47
00:02:59.433 --> 00:03:02.135
Patrick was in the grade below Henry, Cole, and Nathan.

48
00:03:02.155 --> 00:03:04.977
"Hi, Patrick," Henry greeted him.

49
00:03:04.997 --> 00:03:07.379
"Did you enter the art show too?"

50
00:03:07.399 --> 00:03:10.261
"Of course," Patrick said.

51
00:03:10.281 --> 00:03:12.142
"I enter the show every year.

52
00:03:12.862 --> 00:03:14.804
My painting came in third place last year."

53
00:03:14.824 --> 00:03:18.126
"Wow." Nathan sounded impressed.

54
00:03:19.006 --> 00:03:20.928
"I'd be thrilled to come in third place."

55
00:03:21.952 --> 00:03:23.553
Patrick looked at Nathan's painting.

56
00:03:24.233 --> 00:03:25.594
Henry looked closely too.

57
00:03:26.734 --> 00:03:30.095
Nathan had painted a very good watercolor of a calico cat.

58
00:03:30.116 --> 00:03:35.198
"I'm sorry to say this, Nathan, but you probably won't win," Patrick declared.

59
00:03:35.218 --> 00:03:38.659
"Art judges don't usually like pictures of animals."

60
00:03:39.760 --> 00:03:40.660
Maggie frowned.

61
00:03:40.680 --> 00:03:43.821
"I think Nathan's cat painting is amazing!"

62
00:03:44.802 --> 00:03:45.602
Nora looked up.

63
00:03:45.622 --> 00:03:48.183
"Are you talking about my kitty?"

64
00:03:48.203 --> 00:03:50.024
"Your kitty?"

65
00:03:50.728 --> 00:03:52.189
Henry looked at the painting again.

66
00:03:52.209 --> 00:03:54.131
"Oh, I get it.

67
00:03:54.671 --> 00:03:56.072
It's a painting of Patches."

68
00:03:56.832 --> 00:03:58.594
That was the name of Nora's pet cat.

69
00:03:59.554 --> 00:04:03.077
"You should try painting a landscape next year, Nathan," Patrick went on.

70
00:04:03.097 --> 00:04:04.758
"That's what I did.

71
00:04:05.458 --> 00:04:07.740
My art teacher thinks I'll win first place this year."

72
00:04:07.760 --> 00:04:11.303
"We'll see about that," Maggie told Patrick.

73
00:04:11.323 --> 00:04:16.546
"If Patches winds up in the museum and your painting doesn't, you'll regret bragging!"

74
00:04:17.507 --> 00:04:18.748
Nora's eyes widened.

75
00:04:19.596 --> 00:04:20.957
"No!" she blurted out.

76
00:04:20.977 --> 00:04:23.479
"Patches can't live in the museum.

77
00:04:23.919 --> 00:04:25.760
She lives in my room with me!"

78
00:04:25.780 --> 00:04:28.422
"Don't worry," Henry told her.

79
00:04:28.442 --> 00:04:32.845
"We're not talking about sending Patches away to live in the museum.

80
00:04:33.486 --> 00:04:34.626
Just the painting of her."

81
00:04:35.827 --> 00:04:37.148
Nora still looked upset.

82
00:04:37.168 --> 00:04:41.471
"Nathan said I could hang the painting in my room after the show.

83
00:04:42.712 --> 00:04:45.674
She's my kitty, so I should have the painting!"

84
00:04:45.694 --> 00:04:48.776
"It's okay, Nora," Nathan said.

85
00:04:49.500 --> 00:04:51.581
"I'm sure my painting won't win anyway."

86
00:04:52.822 --> 00:04:54.783
Just then another kid ran up to them.

87
00:04:55.564 --> 00:04:58.145
His name was Owen, and he was one of Patrick's friends.

88
00:04:58.165 --> 00:05:00.267
"Guess what, you guys?"

89
00:05:00.607 --> 00:05:01.187
Owen said.

90
00:05:01.807 --> 00:05:03.528
He stopped to take a big breath.

91
00:05:03.548 --> 00:05:07.551
"I just heard the judges talking about the paintings they liked!"

92
00:05:08.591 --> 00:05:10.733
"Really?" Nathan sounded surprised.

93
00:05:10.753 --> 00:05:14.495
"I thought judging didn't start until two o'clock."

94
00:05:15.476 --> 00:05:15.956
"It doesn't.

95
00:05:16.748 --> 00:05:20.551
But I guess they walked through the show and saw some of the artwork already," Owen said.

96
00:05:20.571 --> 00:05:25.474
"All three judges were talking about how good Nathan's cat painting is.

97
00:05:26.535 --> 00:05:27.696
It sounds like he might win!"
